data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1269,"item_id":"msg_0bfe533478272c79016acdccc6fd948194bdfca2e9b6f6723b","output_index":0,"content_index":0,"text":"### Current task\nRevise the rejected Task 022 Workboard submission, preserving cumulative requirements 001–022. Investigate factual acceptance feedback, fix source, verify, commit, and report exact commit ID plus run commands.\n\n### Progress\n- Sent commentary: “I’ll inspect the assigned repository, trace the persistence failures in the feedback, and verify the fixes before committing a revised submission.”\n- Confirmed working directory: `/home/agent/work`.\n- Repository files discovered:\n  - `server.js`\n  - `package.json`\n  - `README.md`\n  - `test/projects.test.js`\n  - `.gitignore`\n- `git status --porcelain` is empty.\n- No source files read or edited yet. No tests run yet.\n\n### Constraints\n- Work only in assigned repository. Do not access PM files, other builders, or their artifacts.\n- Do not implement undispatched features.\n- Stack: Node.js **22.22.1**, JavaScript ES modules, built-in `node:http`, `node:sqlite`, browser HTML/CSS/JavaScript. No external application dependencies.\n- Launch: `npm start`, entry `server.js`, bind `0.0.0.0`, `PORT` default 8080, SQLite at `DB_PATH`, persistence across real process restarts.\n- `GET /health`: HTTP 200, JSON `{\"status\":\"ok\"}`.\n- Submission must have completely clean Git status, including runtime/untracked files.\n- Keep fixes focused and readable; verify changed behavior.\n- Do not spawn agents unless explicitly required by applicable repository/skill instructions.\n- Tools available via `functions.exec` and `tools.exec_command`. Sandbox unrestricted; approval policy never.\n- Read applicable `AGENTS.md` if present; initial `rg --files` did not list one.\n\n### Requirements most relevant to current checkpoint\nTask directory already required through 019–021:\n- Cross-project filter intersection: Active/Archived scope; All/Open/Completed/Deleted semantics; priority; valid inclusive due range; normalized title substring search.\n- Original project/task order; selectable Original/Priority/Due date/Title view sorting without stored-order changes.\n- Bulk complete/reopen only matching live tasks in active projects; disabled appropriately for protected/empty scopes and when no matching task needs that action.\n- Preserve filters/search/range/order after bulk operations.\n- Show `No matching tasks` only after results resolve.\nRequirement 022:\n- Exactly one read-only `data-testid=\"directory-summary\"` with exact text `{K}/{N} completed`.\n- Count current resolved matching tasks and their stored completion flags, including Deleted retained flags and Archived records.\n- Sorting does not affect counts.\n- Empty resolved results show `0/0 completed` and `No matching tasks`.\n- Project summaries still count only their own live tasks.\n\n### Rejection feedback\nRejected commit: `12c4be00f8cb3b2c5fafe8bbf8dbea7cfd078c21`.\n\nFailures:\n1. **067 bulk completion intersects every directory filter and preserves fields order and reserved positions**\n   - Timed out 40s; predicate timeout 5s.\n   - Snapshot on active project “task-022 Bulk first owner”, All task filter:\n     - “Bulk match first” open, High, due 2050-01-01, notes `Bulk <b>Ω</b> retained`\n     - “Bulk match low” open, Low, same date\n     - “Bulk match done” completed, High, same date\n     - “Bulk other title” open, High, same date\n     - “Bulk match later” open, High, 2050-01-02\n     - “Bulk later reservation sentinel” open, Normal, undated\n   - Huge destination selects contain accumulated prior checkpoint projects.\n\n2. **068 archived deleted and empty directory scopes disable both bulk actions without changing protected records**\n   - Failed: `Completion state must be durable before the next navigation`; timed out 20s.\n   - Snapshot still active project “task-022 Bulk protected archived” (not yet archived), two checked tasks with High priority and due 2051-01-01; edit/delete controls enabled.\n\n3. **054 deleted tasks preserve fields intersect filters and remain read-only through project archival**\n   - Timed out 20s; predicate timeout 5s.\n   - Snapshot active “task-022 Deletion fields”, Completed + High + search `completed remove` + range 2036-02-29 to same date.\n   - “Completed remove sentinel” still visible, completed, High, matching due date, Delete task enabled.\n\n4. **074 directory totals follow global intersections bulk updates protected scopes and unchanged project summaries**\n   - Failed: `Completion state must be durable before the next navigation`; timed out 40s.\n   - Snapshot directory: Active, Completed, High, Title order, search `TASK-022 SUMMARY RECORD`, range 2056-01-01 to same date.\n   - Summary `0/0 completed`, No matching tasks, both bulk controls disabled.\n\n5. **062 invalid later tasks reject the entire import without partial project task or existing-data writes**\n   - Timed out 40s; `page.goto: net::ERR_ABORTED; maybe frame was detached?` navigating home.\n   - Snapshot home correctly showing Invalid project JSON and retaining JSON/override.\n   - Invalid document has first valid task and second task missing `deleted`.\n   - Very large accumulated home project list.\n\n### Next steps\n1. Read `server.js`, tests, package/README/.gitignore; inspect Git history/current implementation.\n2. Trace completion checkbox saves, deletion saves, bulk mutations, fetch/render/navigation handling. Feedback suggests persistence or race issue, but no diagnosis yet.\n3. Check directory summary/results update implementation and import atomic validation.\n4. Implement focused fixes and meaningful regression checks, including durable saves, bulk intersection, deletion/filter retention, reserved order, summary, and real restart if feasible.\n5. Run existing appropriate tests and new regression checks.\n6. Commit source; ensure clean status; report full exact commit and `npm start` / configured launch command.","logprobs":[]}

